@startuml
title S3 - Return: proposed interaction contract
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
hide footbox
actor Student
boundary UI
control Reservation
control Core
control "Allocation (M4)" as Allocation
Student -> UI: Confirm return Hub
UI -> Reservation: trip ID, Hub, optional parking hold, version, key
Reservation -> Core: Authenticated return intent
Core -> Core: Authenticate; replay lookup; validate Trip ownership
alt Replay / already completed with same actor and context
  Core --> Reservation: Original receipt / ALREADY_COMPLETED; no movement
else Invalid owner, state, destination or stale version
  Core --> Reservation: Error; Trip and location unchanged
else Owned Active rental and open Trip
  group Atomic return under Core serialization
    Core -> Core: Recheck Hub; consume own valid hold or select\nempty unclaimed space without conflicting future claim
    alt Receiving space exists
      Core -> Core: Occupy destination and set vehicle location\nTrip Completed; Reservation Completed\nConsume matching return-parking hold\nVehicle Returned (Maintenance if fault); persist result/event
      Core --> Reservation: Return receipt and actual time / Hub
    else No usable parking / concurrent capacity loss
      Core --> Reservation: NO_PARKING / CONFLICT; no return writes
    end
  end
  opt Return rejected for capacity
    Reservation -> Core: Query alternative Hubs (no mutation)
    Core -> Allocation: Rank currently feasible Hubs per UC-M4-05
    Allocation --> Core: Candidates + as_of, or none / unavailable
    Core --> Reservation: Advisory alternatives; zero holds
  end
end
Reservation --> UI: Receipt or error + advisory alternatives
UI --> Student: Complete, or select and confirm another Hub
note over Reservation,Core
  No space means rental remains Active and Trip remains open.
  Post-commit Core / M3 readiness is separate from ending the Trip.
  A failed notification never undoes a committed return.
end note
@enduml
